@mcrumiller I also tried on release mode, still much slower:

![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/402a1924-dd2b-4095-a1c1-b2781d01f051)


I will try to add only those that perform better.

@nameexhaustion you were right - with NULLS it's much more efficient.

Regarding implementation, it seems `len()`, `sum()` and `count()` are not regular `FunctionExpr`, and I am struggling finding the right place of the change.

For instance, for the `pl.first().drop_nulls().len()` expression, I looked at the `Arena<AExpr>` supplied to the `optimize_functions` function, which looks -
```
Arena {
    version: 4,
    items: [
        Column(
            "literal",
        ),
        Function {
            input: [
                ExprIR {
                    output_name: ColumnLhs(
                        "literal",
                    ),
                    node: Node(
                        0,
                    ),
                },
            ],
            function: DropNulls,
            options: FunctionOptions {
                collect_groups: GroupWise,
                fmt_str: "",
                cast_to_supertypes: None,
                check_lengths: UnsafeBool(
                    true,
                ),
                flags: FunctionFlags(
                    ALLOW_GROUP_AWARE | ALLOW_EMPTY_INPUTS,
                ),
            },
        },
        Agg(
            Count(
                Node(
                    1,
                ),
                true,
            ),
        ),
    ],
}
```

And it seems like the `len()` is translated to the `AExpr` of:
```
Agg(
    Count(
        Node(
            1,
        ),
        true,
    ),
)
```

But I am not sure what is the right place to modify it.

Thanks.
